WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.640
- Welcome back everybody!

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:04.440
We have Daniel Radcliffe and
Jane Krakowski on the line.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.807
They are both actually in the new

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:08.370
"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt:
Kimmy vs. the Reverend"

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.550
now on Netflix., you gotta check it out.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.090
Because the new "Kimmy Schmidt" episode

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.470
is about making choices,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:17.150
and because Twitter forces tough
questions upon us everyday,

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.670
Daniel, Jane, and I are going to deal

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.620
with some of those very tough choices,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.440
in a little segment called,

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.760
Kelly's Quaran Twitter Questionnaire.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.351
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:27.351 --> 00:00:29.750
I'll read some of the most
liked and retweeted questions

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:30.930
on twitter in the last month,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.490
then we will all get to answer.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:36.297
So, our first Twitter question
is from @theyearofelan

00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:39.497
"Your quarantine nickname
is how you feel right now

00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:42.520
"plus the last thing you
ate out of a cupboard."

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.910
Okay Jane, you go, ladies first, go ahead.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.910
- Okay, mine would be hopeful Nut Thins.

00:00:49.959 --> 00:00:54.230
- (laughs) That's amazing!

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:55.260
Daniel, what's yours?

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.870
- I was gonna say, mine
I guess would be like,

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.660
contented honey roasted almonds.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.950
It's quite long.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.167
- I like that though.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:06.400
- Okay, mine is overwhelmed
red velvet cake. (laughs)

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.428
(laughing)

00:01:08.428 --> 00:01:10.450
But, you know what, you
usually do feel overwhelmed

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.210
when you eat too much
of it, a friend told me,

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.970
I obviously haven't eaten too much.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.670
All right, so next question,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.670
next twitter question is from @GifMario.

00:01:21.027 --> 00:01:25.477
"Who is your racer of choice
in Mario Kart on Nintendo 64?"

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:27.840
Daniel, what's yours?

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:28.730
You're the gamer.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.820
- I was never very good at it,

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.540
but I think that character
that I always liked

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.620
playing as the most was Yoshi.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.453
- I love Yoshi!

00:01:35.453 --> 00:01:36.286
- I think I would go with that

00:01:36.286 --> 00:01:37.950
just because he was cute and fun.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.240
- Yeah, Yoshi was cool.
- (mumbles).

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.030
- That would've been mine, Yoshi's mine.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.028
What's yours Jane, have
you ever played Mario Kart?

00:01:44.028 --> 00:01:45.330
- (laughs) I've never played it.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.270
I somehow, did not get into
the video games thing at all,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.870
and I know, with kids, the kid pressure,

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.750
my son hasn't really gotten
into them yet either,

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.460
I'm like sorta trying to slow that down,

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:58.169
but so like, I'll take Yoshi too (laughs).

00:01:58.169 --> 00:02:00.046
- Yoshi's awesome!

00:02:00.046 --> 00:02:00.879
Yoshi's, It's a fun one.

00:02:00.879 --> 00:02:05.772
Okay, this next one was
posted by @movingsideways,

00:02:05.772 --> 00:02:08.277
"You are quarantined with the first artist

00:02:08.277 --> 00:02:09.597
"you saw in concert.

00:02:09.597 --> 00:02:10.790
"Who is it?"

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.390
- Daniel, I'll let you go first.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.210
- Well, the first band I
went to see was The Strokes.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:21.750
Which is quite cool, but,
the actual real answer

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:25.250
which is that a concert I was
taken to when I was like 10

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.900
would be the Pet Shop Boys.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.216
So, it would be me and the Pet Shop Boys.

00:02:28.216 --> 00:02:29.592
- Wow!

00:02:29.592 --> 00:02:30.810
Those are both pretty cool.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.390
- Yeah, they're both pretty cool.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.976
- Yeah, okay, you're cool, whatever, cool.

00:02:34.976 --> 00:02:36.753
What was yours Jane?

00:02:36.753 --> 00:02:39.413
- Mine's a little more
Jersey, where I was raised.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.690
Mine is Van Halen. (laughs)

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.361
- Oh that's amazing! (laughs)

00:02:44.361 --> 00:02:45.610
- [Daniel] That would be
a hell of a quarantine.

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:48.530
- So me and David Lee Roth
like dancing on our table,

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.070
like, I guess, I don't know. (laughs)

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.860
- Your quarantine's gonna be a good time!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.750
That's amazing-

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.527
- My house is gonna be trashed!

00:02:55.527 --> 00:02:59.011
(laughing loudly)

00:02:59.011 --> 00:02:59.844
What's yours Kelly?
- Mine,

00:02:59.844 --> 00:03:02.410
I honestly can't remember,
I know this sounds funny,

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:07.410
I can't remember, it was either,
this is gonna sound funny,

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.450
but it was either the Toadies,

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.690
which is my favorite band of all time,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.790
it's a Texas band, they're alternative.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.560
Or, it's Celine Dion,

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.800
so I don't know which one it is. (laughs)

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.103
But I think, she'd be a hell
of a good time in a quarantine,

00:03:20.103 --> 00:03:20.959
because
- I think so too.

00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:22.330
I don't know if you've seen her on stage,

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.853
but she is crazy funny.

